{
  "adaptations": [
    "Court code is packaged as potofgold.multi_agent. Strategy parsing, readouts, preparation and replay use potofgold.evolutionary_search. Original source identities are retained below.",
    "The package includes the original development/test membership and calendar. New-run fingerprints cover court code, prompts, shared GP code and input files.",
    "New assessments use prosecution, defense and three judges. The optional analyst and its additional judging pass are omitted. The extra mechanism guide is also omitted. Historical prompt identities, decisions and transcripts are retained.",
    "Prompts are defined in assessment/prompts.py. Court and single-LLM execution share strategy profiles, validated measurements, reference findings and diagnostic tools.",
    "Preparation accepts caller-supplied market inputs, fits lean readouts on training rows and supports optional ridge target residualization. CAT_RUNNER_VIX_STATE supplies the recorded 10:30 volatility inputs.",
    "POTOFGOLD_COURT_WORKSPACE and POTOFGOLD_COURT_AUDIT_DIR configure runtime locations. The CLI accepts a YAML argument preset and supplies preparation, assessment, outcome evaluation and report commands.",
    "The release contains the H3 assessment paths and diagnostic dependencies. Retired campaigns, calibration workflows, alternate allocation modes, duplicated GP replay code and optional news extraction are omitted. Historical profile fields remain readable.",
    "New assessments obtain reference rules from evidence_store.json. Reference construction remains available for new development populations; separate per-condition calibration files are omitted.",
    "Four preparation dependencies were untracked in the research checkout. Their source_origin records identify working-tree snapshots rather than frozen-commit files.",
    "Comments and docstrings describe the current implementation. Two unused helpers were removed: the legacy context-only citation validator and terminal-threshold conversion utility. Executable prompts and archived research records are unchanged by these edits."
  ],
